# Kolsch reads secrets from `.env` via the dotenv secrets provider
# (docs/how-to/connect-a-provider.md). You don't need to hand-populate
# this file for normal use — `kolsch connect <provider>` writes its
# own `<PROVIDER_NAME_UPPER>_API_KEY` line here automatically.
#
# Uncomment and fill in to skip the interactive connect prompt:
# OPENROUTER_API_KEY=sk-or-...
# OPENCODE_API_KEY=...

# The `pytest -m e2e` suite (tests/e2e/test_e2e.py) needs real
# infrastructure and is skipped by default. Set these only if you're
# running that suite locally:
# E2E_LLM_API_KEY=...
# E2E_LLM_PROVIDER=openrouter
# E2E_SOAK_MINUTES=5
# E2E_DEFAULT_INSTALL=1
